{%- comment -%}
  Section header: an optional embroidery motif, an optional small label (eyebrow), a heading
  and an optional subtitle. One place for how a home page section introduces itself, so the
  sections read as one page.

  Parameters:
    motif           (optional) name of an embroidery motif (snippets/embroidery-motif.liquid),
                    drawn small above the eyebrow in ink-muted, centered like the
                    header (at the start when align is 'left'). Decoration only: it
                    is aria-hidden and the section must read the same without it. A blank or
                    unknown name renders nothing.
    eyebrow         (optional) small label above the heading, label style, brand color.
    heading         (optional) the heading text.
    heading_accent  (optional) a second part of the heading, shown after a space in the brand
                    color. Plain text: both parts are separate settings, no markup in copy.
                    The space is always emitted, see the whitespace trap note in the h tag.
    subtitle        (optional) paragraph under the heading, body-lg, ink.
    level           (optional) heading level, 1 to 6. Default 2. The size does not change with
                    the level: the caller picks the level that fits the page outline.
    align           (optional) 'center' (default) or 'left'.
    class           (optional) extra classes for spacing, never for color.

  Nothing renders when eyebrow, heading, heading_accent and subtitle are all blank (a motif
  alone is not a header).
  The brand color is used for text on bg and bg-raised only (5.2 to 1 on bg, more on
  bg-raised), never on a line color or on a photograph.

  Usage:
    {% render 'section-header', heading: section.settings.heading, level: 2 %}
    {% render 'section-header', eyebrow: 'x', heading: 'y', heading_accent: 'z', align: 'left' %}
    {% render 'section-header', motif: 'ola-suave', eyebrow: 'x', heading: 'y' %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign header_level = level | default: 2 | plus: 0
  if header_level < 1 or header_level > 6
    assign header_level = 2
  endif

  assign header_align = 'center'
  if align == 'left'
    assign header_align = 'left'
  endif

  assign header_classes = 'section-header section-header--' | append: header_align
  if class != blank
    assign header_classes = header_classes | append: ' ' | append: class
  endif
-%}

{%- if eyebrow != blank or heading != blank or heading_accent != blank or subtitle != blank -%}
  {{ 'component-section-header.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

  {%- comment -%}
    The motif is captured first so that an unknown name, for which the motif snippet renders
    nothing, leaves no empty box (and no extra gap) behind.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- capture header_motif -%}
    {%- if motif != blank -%}{% render 'embroidery-motif', name: motif, size: 40 %}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endcapture -%}

  <div class="{{ header_classes }}">
    {%- if header_motif != blank -%}
      <div class="section-header__motif">{{ header_motif }}</div>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if eyebrow != blank -%}
      <p class="section-header__eyebrow text-label">{{ eyebrow }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if heading != blank or heading_accent != blank -%}
      <h{{ header_level }} class="section-header__heading text-display-md">
        {%- comment -%}
          WHITESPACE TRAP: the gap between heading and accent must come from an output tag
          that prints a space string, never from a bare space typed between two tags.
          A bare space is plain template text, and whitespace control (the dash on a tag
          delimiter, here on the tag that opens the next line) trims plain text beside it,
          so the space can go with the newline and the words render joined ("mirarel mar").
          The value an output tag prints is not template text, so no dash can trim it.
          Do not turn the output tag below back into a typed space.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if heading != blank -%}{{ heading }}{%- endif -%}
        {%- if heading != blank and heading_accent != blank -%}{{ ' ' }}{%- endif -%}
        {%- if heading_accent != blank -%}<span class="section-header__accent">{{ heading_accent }}</span>{%- endif -%}
      </h{{ header_level }}>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if subtitle != blank -%}
      <p class="section-header__subtitle text-body-lg">{{ subtitle }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
